From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:58:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 332/342] media: log lost audio to the syslog, not to an unread
 stderr

USB audio on a C2 on Wi-Fi still stutters a few times a song with every
packet reaching the adapter on time, so the audio is lost before the
driver; the media add-ons said so only on media_addon_server's stdout and
stderr, which nobody reads. Now in the syslog: the multi_audio node's
buffers dropped late or because the one before wasn't played yet, and
slots it filled with silence for want of a buffer (at most once a second,
with a count, while running); the mixer's input glitches (a buffer not
where the last one ended) and the late notices it gets.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../media/media-add-ons/mixer/AudioMixer.cpp  |  5 +--
 .../media/media-add-ons/mixer/MixerInput.cpp  | 11 ++++---
 .../multi_audio/MultiAudioNode.cpp            | 33 ++++++++++++++++---
 3 files changed, 38 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

